{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "FireAtmosphereColumnLastChance",
  "description": "The fire -> atmosphere half of EqAtmFire verified against a REAL coupled WRF + CFBM run, not a WRF-SFIRE archive. Same three-stage chain as couplings/fire_atmosphere_column.esm -- Anderson-13 fuel table -> Calc_fire_fluxes (FireHeatFlux) for the fire cell -> Provide_atm_feedback aggregation and Fire_tendency column distribution (FireFluxToAtmosphereWRFFire) -- but the regime is domain 5 of the Last Chance Gulch case (2012-06-25, 300 x 450 x 50 at dx = 100 m, sr_x = sr_y = 4, ifire = 1, fire_atm_feedback = 1, dt = 0.5 s), WRF column (i = 167, j = 69) at 18:10 UTC, five minutes after ignition, where GRNHFX peaks at 255 kW/m^2. The old document's reference is test7/wrf.nc, which FORTRAN_BUGS N52 records was produced by WRF-SFIRE (ifire = 2) and not by the CFBM this repo transcribes; this one closes that gap. WHAT THE REPLAY ESTABLISHED, measured: (1) Calc_fire_fluxes reproduces the run's own fire-mesh flux from fuel_frac_burnt_dt, the Anderson fgi of the cell's category and fmc_g to 1.1e-7 relative over all 1117 burning fire cells of the frame, with five fuel categories live (1, 2, 5, 8, 9); (2) the Provide_atm_feedback block mean reproduces the run's own GRNHFX/GRNQFX to 2.1e-7 relative over the 138 atmosphere cells with GRNHFX > 1 kW/m^2, which fixes the fire-to-atmosphere index mapping (fire cell (4a + ci, 4b + cj), 0-based) beyond doubt; (3) Fire_tendency, replayed in Fortran by data/eqwefic/fire_build/lastchance_feedback/lastchance_feedback_driver on the extracted 7 x 7 x 50 tile, reproduces WRF's own in-run RTHFRTEN column to 1.5e2 Pa K/s out of 3.3e5, i.e. 4.5e-4 relative, and RQVFRTEN to the same 4.5e-4. That residual is NOT a transcription error: it is the half-step state offset. RTHFRTEN is computed in Runge-Kutta step 1 from the rho, z_at_w and mut the step STARTS with, while wrfout stores the state the step ENDS with, and a 0.5 s step of a column heated at 4 K/s moves rho dz by that much. The evidence is that the heat and moisture residuals are the SAME relative number to seven digits -- a pure geometry factor, not a flux error -- and that the two independent reconstructions of rho (the WRF dry equation of state, and the mass-coordinate identity -(c1h mut + c2h) dnw = rho_d g dz8w) agree to 1e-5 in the lower twenty layers. The test therefore asserts the column twice: against the Fortran driver at 1e-5 (transcription), and against WRF's own stored RTHFRTEN at the measured 4.5e-4 (end-to-end closure). fire_rain is identically zero over the whole 12-hour fire, so this case says nothing about the fuel-moisture wetting branch.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "assembly",
   "coupling",
   "wildland_fire",
   "fire_behavior"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Coupled WRF 4.8 + NCAR fire_behavior (CFBM, ifire = 1) run of the Last Chance Gulch fire, data/eqwefic/lastchance/runs/full, domain 5, wrfout_d05_2012-06-25_18:10:00 and fire_output_2012-06-25_18:10:00.nc. Offline replay of io/wrf_mod.F90 Provide_atm_feedback/Fire_tendency by data/eqwefic/fire_build/lastchance_feedback/lastchance_feedback_driver against libfirelib of fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior @ 8d519c6, real32."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 50,
   "description": "Atmosphere layers of the Last Chance domain-5 column (e_vert = 51, so kte = 50)."
  },
  "NSUB": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Fire cells per atmosphere cell, sr_x sr_y = 16."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "Fuel": {
   "ref": "../components/wildland_fire/fire_behavior/anderson13_fuel_table.esm"
  },
  "HeatFlux": {
   "ref": "../components/wildland_fire/level_set/fire_heat_flux.esm"
  },
  "Flux": {
   "ref": "../components/wildland_fire/fire_behavior/fire_flux_to_atmosphere_wrffire.esm",
   "bindings": {
    "NLEV": "NLEV",
    "NSUB": "NSUB"
   },
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "../components/wildland_fire/fire_behavior/tests/lastchance_1810_col_166_68_inputs.esm"
    }
   ]
  },
  "FireAtmosphereColumnLastChance": {
   "variables": {
    "code": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "Prescribed: Anderson fuel category of the coupled fire cell (nfuel_cat = 2 over the whole 4 x 4 block)."},
    "fuel_burn_rate": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1/s", "description": "Prescribed: fuel consumption rate of the coupled fire cell, fuel_frac_burnt_dt / dt with dt = 0.5 s from namelist.cfbm."},
    "M_f": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "Prescribed: fuel moisture of the coupled fire cell (fmc_g; the run has fmoist_run off, so it stays at the 0.08 initial value)."},
    "h_fuel": {"type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg", "description": "Prescribed: heat of combustion of dry fuel (CMBCNST)."},
    "L_water": {"type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg", "description": "Prescribed: latent heat of vaporisation (XLV)."},
    "s_coupled": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "Prescribed: Fortran-order index (1-based) within the 4 x 4 block of the fire cell the chain computes; cell 10, the strongest of the block, at fire mesh (666, 275) 1-based."},
    "mu": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "description": "Prescribed: dry air mass of the column, WRF mut = MU + MUB."},
    "fgi_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "kg/m^2", "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Fuel.fgi."},
    "phi_h_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "W/m^2", "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives HeatFlux.phi_h."},
    "phi_q_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "W/m^2", "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives HeatFlux.phi_q."},
    "grnhfx_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "W/m^2", "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Flux.grnhfx."},
    "grnqfx_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "W/m^2", "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Flux.grnqfx."},
    "rthfrten_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa*K/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Flux.rthfrten_wrf."},
    "rqvfrten_in": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa/s", "shape": ["lev"], "default": 0.0, "description": "Receives Flux.rqvfrten_wrf."},
    "fgi": {"type": "unknown", "units": "kg/m^2", "description": "Oven-dry surface fuel load of the cell's category, the load Calc_fire_fluxes uses."},
    "phi_h": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2", "description": "Sensible heat flux of the coupled fire cell (fire_behavior fgrnhfx)."},
    "phi_q": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2", "description": "Latent heat flux of the coupled fire cell (fgrnqfx)."},
    "grnhfx": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2", "description": "Atmosphere-cell sensible heat flux, the mean of the 16 fire cells (WRF GRNHFX)."},
    "grnqfx": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2", "description": "Atmosphere-cell latent heat flux (WRF GRNQFX)."},
    "rthfrten": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa*K/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "TENDENCY: the mass-weighted potential-temperature tendency column (WRF RTHFRTEN)."},
    "rqvfrten": {"type": "unknown", "units": "Pa/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "TENDENCY: the mass-weighted water-vapour tendency column (WRF RQVFRTEN)."}
   },
   "equations": [
    {"lhs": "code", "rhs": 2.0},
    {"lhs": "fuel_burn_rate", "rhs": 0.0908107758},
    {"lhs": "M_f", "rhs": 0.0799999982118607},
    {"lhs": "h_fuel", "rhs": 17433000.0},
    {"lhs": "L_water", "rhs": 2500000.0},
    {"lhs": "s_coupled", "rhs": 10.0},
    {"lhs": "mu", "rhs": 79419.4140625},
    {"lhs": "fgi", "rhs": "fgi_in"},
    {"lhs": "phi_h", "rhs": "phi_h_in"},
    {"lhs": "phi_q", "rhs": "phi_q_in"},
    {"lhs": "grnhfx", "rhs": "grnhfx_in"},
    {"lhs": "grnqfx", "rhs": "grnqfx_in"},
    {"lhs": "rthfrten", "rhs": "rthfrten_in"},
    {"lhs": "rqvfrten", "rhs": "rqvfrten_in"}
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "lastchance_d05_1810_col_166_68",
     "description": "Reference: the coupled Last Chance Gulch WRF + CFBM run at 2012-06-25 18:10 UTC, domain 5, WRF column (i = 167, j = 69) 1-based, fire cell (666, 275) 1-based. phi_h/phi_q are the run's own fire_output fgrnhfx/fgrnqfx; grnhfx/grnqfx and the two tendency columns are the offline Fortran replay of Provide_atm_feedback/Fire_tendency on the state extracted from wrfout at that time (lastchance_feedback_driver). Single precision throughout: rel 1e-5. The SECOND pair of column assertions compares the same tendencies against WRF's OWN stored RTHFRTEN/RQVFRTEN, at the measured half-step offset of 1.5e2 Pa K/s (4.5e-4 of the column maximum) and 5.5e-3 Pa/s -- that is an end-to-end closure check against the coupled model, not a transcription check, and its tolerance records what was measured rather than certifying agreement.",
     "parameter_overrides": {},
     "time_span": {"start": 0, "end": 1},
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "fgi", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.8960000276565552, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "phi_h", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1313390.25, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "phi_q", "time": 0.0, "expected": 120542.8984375, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "grnhfx", "time": 0.0, "expected": 255032.40625, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "grnqfx", "time": 0.0, "expected": 23406.8671875, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "rthfrten", "time": 0.0, "coords": {"lev": 1}, "expected": 327087.625, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "rthfrten", "time": 0.0, "coords": {"lev": 2}, "expected": 154195.984375, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "rthfrten", "time": 0.0, "coords": {"lev": 5}, "expected": 8009.94482421875, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "rthfrten", "time": 0.0, "coords": {"lev": 10}, "expected": 0.7491570115089417, "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-05}},
      {"variable": "rthfrten", "time": 0.0, "coords": {"lev": 50}, "expected": 0.0, "tolerance": {"abs": 1e-12}},
